WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.200
Over two thousand migrants and refugees from&nbsp;
Haiti, South and Central America are making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.280
the desperate journey north--from&nbsp;
southern Mexico to the US border.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.400
Many of them were stranded in Mexico&nbsp;
for months waiting for their asylum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.400
claims to be processed--before deciding&nbsp;
to take matters into their own hands.&nbsp;

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.240
Thousands of refugees and migrants&nbsp;
trekking by foot out of southern Mexico.&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.120
This is one of many caravans&nbsp;
where people join together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.800
with hopes of getting to the United States.
Most of them from Haiti, Honduras and El Salvador&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:38.160
have been waiting here for asylum papers to be&nbsp;
processed. But now say, they've lost patience.&nbsp;

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.880
"Many Nicaraguans have been detained&nbsp;
here for 6, 7 or 8 months…we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.440
been locked up here for a long&nbsp;
time, we can`t take it anymore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.920
We don`t have work here, we can`t live. In&nbsp;
our country it is much worse. So we need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.240
get out of here to feed our families, our&nbsp;
children who are the future of tomorrow."&nbsp;

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:06.960
Men, women and children walked along&nbsp;
a highway from the city of Tapachula&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.240
near the Guatemala border toward Mexico's capital.&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.800
Some were confronted by police trying&nbsp;
to push them back. Mexican authorities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:24.880
say anyone trying to leave the city could&nbsp;
be penalized and is urging people to stay.&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.520
"What happens is that the migrants have&nbsp;
been badly informed. They deceive them. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.680
right now no judge has given a resolution&nbsp;
for them to pass through freely. We are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:41.760
going to invite them to stay."
Others prayed overnight before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.760
making the journey toward the US.&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.800
"We can`t take it anymore, this is&nbsp;
like a bomb, like an explosive bomb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:00.240
we`ve already exploded. We want to get&nbsp;
out of here, we can`t take it anymore."&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.320
Many are fleeing political crisis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.840
economic turmoil and natural&nbsp;
disasters in their home countries.&nbsp;

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:14.480
But the Biden Administration is looking at&nbsp;
measures to stop illegal entries. This year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:21.120
US authorities have reportedly already detained&nbsp;
1.7 million migrants trying to cross its border.&nbsp;

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:26.320
Just last month, thousands of mainly&nbsp;
Haitians arrived at Del Rio, Texas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.960
According to rights groups, the US&nbsp;
government expelled nearly 8000 of them.&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:35.920
But for many of these people&nbsp;
making the harrowing journey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:48.240
it’s a risk they're willing to&nbsp;
take in search of a better life.

